  "evidence": [
    "Current draw_unit and draw_ability historical missing-destructor notes are superseded by genuine StringList/StringStruct destructor stages. No class migration or broad lifetime rewrite is authorized.",
    "draw_chassis42D610: retain early explicit reset at original42D7CA; after soft_update42DD96, original42DD9E enters derived table6698C4 cleanup, then42DE27 base table6693A4 cleanup. Remove only the trailing explicit source reset.",
    "draw_weapon42E2E0: retain pre-load clear, originally inlined42E60C..42E668. After write_strings42E6F6 original continues title/detail/show/soft_update42E77A before derived42E782 and base42E80B teardown stages. Remove source reset immediately after write_strings; no fourth cleanup traversal exists in original.",
    "Keep original renderer distinctions: unit, chassis, defense and ability each have one explicit clear, reactor two, weapon one pre-load inlined clear. Direct-call absence alone is not evidence of absent cleanup. No StringList owner edits or intentional bug fixes.",
    "Test actual source body ordering and retained explicit reset counts against pinned disassembly controls; preserve historical identities and claims. Measure entire Datalink TU, inspect changed code/EH effects, fresh build/link and claims/references before serial manual integration. Existing unsupported cold-EH comparison remains unknown, not a pass.",
    "Parallel helper batch edits distinct files but shares a read-only consumer measurement closure. Keep builds/worktrees/prefixes isolated; integrate serially and verify combined state."
  ],
